  "era": "jesus",
  "lifespan": "73–4 BC",
  "summary": "Herod was king of Judea under Roman rule. He is known for massive building projects, including the expansion of the Temple in Jerusalem, but also for his brutality and paranoia. He is infamous for the massacre of infants in Bethlehem in an attempt to kill the newborn Messiah.",
